        id: "genre-fantasy",
        summary: "fantasy genre promises and page-level craft guidance.",
        text: "# Fantasy Prose Addendum\n\nFantasy rewards wonder, coherence, texture, and the feeling that the world\nextends beyond the page. The invented world should constrain the scene instead\nof sitting behind it as exposition.\n\n## Protect\n\n- World details that matter to character choice, cost, status, or danger.\n- Terminology introduced through use before explanation when possible.\n- Magic and politics with boundaries, costs, and social consequences.\n- A sense of history without pausing the scene to lecture.\n\n## Common LLM Failure Modes\n\n- Front-loading lore before the reader needs it.\n- Explaining magic as a clean system detached from culture or cost.\n- Using invented terms without enough context to orient.\n- Making every place sound generically ancient, grand, or mystical.\n\n## During Revision\n\nCheck whether each world detail changes the scene pressure. Keep wonder, but\nanchor it in action, consequence, and point of view.",
